Root cause:
The function `fprop_new_period()` in lib/flex_proportions.c used `preempt_disable_nested()` to protect the write-side of a sequence counter, but this only disables preemption, not hardirqs. When a hardirq occurs during the write section (between `write_seqcount_begin` and `write_seqcount_end`), a read-side function (like `fprop_fraction_percpu()`) may read the sequence counter while it has an odd value (indicating a write in progress), causing it to spin indefinitely. This leads to a deadlock/livelock.

Code statements information:
